<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Party (South Africa)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1914">1914</a>–<a href="/years/1997">1997</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Party was a South African political party founded in 1914 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/j-b-m-hertzog">J. B. M. Hertzog</a> to represent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaners">Afrikaner</a> nationalism. After Hertzog's fusion with Smuts in 1934, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/d-f-malan">D. F. Malan</a> led a breakaway Purified National Party, which became the Reunited National Party and won the 1948 election. It governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> until 1994 and built the system of apartheid, which it negotiated away under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/f-w-de-klerk">F. W. de Klerk</a>; renamed the New National Party, it dissolved in 2005.</p></div>
